ModelResponse(id='gen-1767244766-Ien2WxqHnj7x6g9hrzfK', created=1767244766, model='openai/gpt-5.2', object='chat.completion', system_fingerprint=None, choices=[Choices(finish_reason='stop', index=0, message=Message(content='{
  "analysis": "We’ve confirmed the exact input file schemas and installed Java 7. /app/output has been created. H2 is installed from Debian but it’s version 2.x, while the task explicitly requires H2 1.3 DB2 mode and producing a bankdb.h2.db compatible with that format. We need to download an H2 1.3.x jar and then implement BankBatchJob (Java 7) from scratch, compile into /app/job.jar, and run to generate interest.csv, exceptions.csv, stats.json, and bankdb.h2.db deterministically.",
  "plan": "1) Download H2 1.3.176 jar into /app/lib/h2.jar (keeping runtime/compile classpath stable).\n2) Write /app/src/BankBatchJob.java implementing all rules: reversal detection across file, reason precedence, FX selection (direct/reverse/latest<=date, pivots), fee/adjustments, balances/APR/interest, outputs formatting, md5, and H2 DB creation with required JDBC URL containing MODE=DB2 and /app/output/bankdb.\n3) Compile with javac -source/-target 1.7 and build /app/job.jar with manifest including Main-Class=BankBatchJob and Class-Path=lib/h2.jar so `java -jar /app/job.jar` works.\n4) Run the job and inspect outputs quickly (head/cat + md5) to verify formatting (LF + trailing newline for CSVs; stats.json single line no newline).",
